  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>pK</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>logK</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub></math>, here <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub></math> acid dissociation constant. More the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub></math> value, stronger is the acidic nature of the respective acid.</p><p>Hence, the lower <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>pK</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub></math> value denotes a more powerful acid.  Phenols are more acidic than alcohols. Hence, ethanol has more <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>pK</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub></math> value. Nitro group is the electron withdrawing group, hence it increases the acidic nature of phenols.  Among the given phenols para nitrophenol  is stronger acid. The <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>pK</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub></math> values are matched below.</p><p>Ethanol <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>→</mo></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>9</mn></math></p><p>Phenol<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>→</mo><mn>10</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>-</mo></math>Nitrophenol <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>→</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>-</mo></math>Nitrophenol<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>→</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>Hence, the answer is option D.</p>"
  }
}